version: v1alpha1
metadata:
  name: nftables
  version: "{{ .VERSION }}"
  author: slipmesh
  description: |
    Oneshot nftables ruleset loader (restart: never - applies once and exits, no ongoing daemon).
    Reads a raw nftables-syntax ruleset from an ExtensionServiceConfig, substitutes a couple of
    template placeholders for values only knowable on the running node (which interface carries
    the default route, per address family), and applies it via a statically-linked `nft`. Identifies
    its own tables to remove before reapplying by scanning the ruleset itself for `table`
    declarations - not a hardcoded name, and never `flush ruleset` (other nftables users on the same
    node are left alone). See talos-extensions/README.md's nftables section for the full config
    shape and an example ruleset (MSS clamp + NAT of private ranges on egress).
  compatibility:
    talos:
      version: ">= v1.10.0"
